## Description

`pipeline.ts` line 876 uses `deferredWorkerCalls.push(...chunkWorkerData.calls)` which puts every array element on the call stack as a function argument. When `chunkWorkerData.calls` exceeds ~100K entries, this triggers `Maximum call stack size exceeded`.

Discovered while testing #648 on a 78K-file C codebase. The cast-expression fix in #648 increases CALLS edge count significantly, making this crash reproducible.

## Reproduction

1. Index a large C codebase (78K+ files with many function calls)
2. `gitnexus analyze --force`
3. Crashes with: `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded` at `runChunkedParseAndResolve (pipeline.js:652)`

## Affected Lines

`gitnexus/src/core/ingestion/pipeline.ts` — all `push(...spread)` on deferred arrays:
```
deferredWorkerCalls.push(...chunkWorkerData.calls);        // line ~876
deferredWorkerHeritage.push(...chunkWorkerData.heritage);
deferredConstructorBindings.push(...chunkWorkerData.constructorBindings);
deferredAssignments.push(...chunkWorkerData.assignments);
workerTypeEnvBindings.push(...chunkWorkerData.typeEnvBindings);
allFetchCalls.push(...chunkWorkerData.fetchCalls);
allExtractedRoutes.push(...chunkWorkerData.routes);
allDecoratorRoutes.push(...chunkWorkerData.decoratorRoutes);
allToolDefs.push(...chunkWorkerData.toolDefs);
allORMQueries.push(...chunkWorkerData.ormQueries);
allFetchCalls.push(...chunkFetchCalls);
```

## Fix

Replace spread-push with a loop:
```javascript
// Before (crashes on large arrays):
deferredWorkerCalls.push(...chunkWorkerData.calls);

// After:
for (const call of chunkWorkerData.calls) deferredWorkerCalls.push(call);
```

Tested locally: patching all 11 occurrences in `pipeline.js` resolves the crash. 78K-file codebase indexes successfully with 179,952 edges.

