## Summary

`group.yaml` supports a `links` section for declaring explicit cross-repo service dependencies. The YAML is parsed and validated correctly by `config-parser.ts`, but **`syncGroup` in `sync.ts` never reads `config.links`** — so these declarations are silently dropped and produce zero cross-links.

## Root cause

`ManifestExtractor` (`extractors/manifest-extractor.ts`) is fully implemented: it converts manifest `links` into both provider/consumer `StoredContract` pairs and direct `CrossLink` entries with `matchType: 'manifest'`. However, `sync.ts` never imports or calls it.

```ts
// sync.ts imports (v1.6.1)
import { HttpRouteExtractor } from './extractors/http-route-extractor.js';
import { GrpcExtractor } from './extractors/grpc-extractor.js';
import { TopicExtractor } from './extractors/topic-extractor.js';
// ManifestExtractor ← missing
import { runExactMatch } from './matching.js';
```

`dbExecutors` (the per-repo Cypher executor map needed by `ManifestExtractor.resolveSymbol`) is built inside `syncGroup` but never passed anywhere useful. `config.links` is never accessed.

## Impact

This bug is most visible with PHP/Laravel repos where HTTP clients call external services via absolute URLs (e.g. `file_get_contents('https://api.example.com/...')`). The HTTP extractor only emits **providers** (it normalises call URLs starting with `/`), so it can't detect these consumers. The `links` block in `group.yaml` is the only documented workaround, but it silently does nothing.

## Reproduction

1. Create a group with `links` declared in `group.yaml`
2. Run `gitnexus group sync <name>`
3. Observe `crossLinks: 0` regardless of how many links are declared

## Fix

Wire `ManifestExtractor` into `syncGroup`, called **inside the outer `try` block** (after the per-repo loop, before the `finally` closes DB pools) so `resolveSymbol` has open executors for symbol resolution:

```ts
// After the per-repo for loop, still inside try { }
if (config.links.length > 0) {
  const manifestEx = new ManifestExtractor();
  const manifestResult = await manifestEx.extractFromManifest(config.links, dbExecutors);
  autoContracts.push(...manifestResult.contracts);
  manifestCrossLinks = manifestResult.crossLinks;
}
```

Then merge into the final cross-links:
```ts
const crossLinks: CrossLink[] = [...matched, ...manifestCrossLinks];
```

Full patch: https://gist.github.com/jonasvanderhaegen-xve/e2bf066d842f676aa16400e10ae5114f

A PR with the fix is attached.

