## Problem

Running `gitnexus group sync <name>` always produces hundreds of warnings:

```
[manifest-extractor] resolveSymbol failed for http:POST /api/v1/... in backend: LadybugDB not initialized for repo "my-repo". Call initLbug first.
```

This happens on every sync, regardless of repo configuration. Tested on v1.6.4-rc.64 and v1.6.5.

## Root Cause

In `dist/core/group/sync.js`, the `ManifestExtractor` pipeline runs **after** the `try/finally` block that closes all LadybugDB connections:

```javascript
// Line 143-147: connections closed here
finally {
    for (const id of [...new Set(openPoolIds)]) {
        await closeLbug(id).catch(() => { });
    }
}

// ... later, line 186-187: ManifestExtractor tries to use the closed connections
const manifestEx = new ManifestExtractor();
const manifestResult = await manifestEx.extractFromManifest(allLinks, dbExecutors);
```

By the time `ManifestExtractor.extractFromManifest()` calls `resolveSymbol`, the pool entries have already been removed by `closeLbug()`, so `executeParameterized()` throws at pool-adapter.js:460.

The code comment (line 175-177) acknowledges this is intentional:

> "Placed after the DB try/finally: resolveSymbol falls back to synthetic UIDs when dbExecutors is undefined or a pool is closed"

However, this design produces noisy warnings that make it hard to distinguish real errors from expected fallback behavior.

## Impact

- **Functional**: Low — cross-links are still generated using synthetic UIDs
- **UX**: High — hundreds of warning lines on every `group sync`, obscuring actual errors
- **Accuracy**: Medium — cross-links lack precise symbol/line-number resolution

## Suggested Fix

Move `ManifestExtractor` inside the `try` block (before `closeLbug`), so it can resolve symbols against the live DB connections:

```javascript
try {
    // ... existing extraction loop ...

    // Process manifest links while DB is still open
    if (allLinks.length > 0) {
        const manifestEx = new ManifestExtractor();
        const manifestResult = await manifestEx.extractFromManifest(allLinks, dbExecutors);
        autoContracts.push(...manifestResult.contracts);
        manifestCrossLinks = manifestResult.crossLinks;
    }
} finally {
    for (const id of [...new Set(openPoolIds)]) {
        await closeLbug(id).catch(() => { });
    }
}
```

Alternatively, suppress the warnings when fallback to synthetic UIDs is the expected path (e.g., log at `debug` level instead of `warn`).

