## Summary

`populatePhpNamespaceSiblings` in `namespace-siblings.ts` causes OOM (32GB+ heap exhausted) when processing large PHP codebases (16K+ files). The root cause is Step 3b which injects fully-qualified-name (FQN) bindings into **every** PHP file's Module scope — an O(files × classDefs) operation that creates tens of millions of augmentation entries.

This is a separate issue from #1741 (which was OOM in the deferred-calls accumulation phase, fixed by PR #1800). This OOM occurs **after** the #1800 fix, during the PHP scope-resolution phase.

## Environment

- **GitNexus:** 1.6.5 with PR #1800 patches applied
- **Platform:** Linux x64, Node v24.16.0, DDEV container
- **Heap:** 32GB (`--max-old-space-size=32768`), 62GB RAM available
- **Project:** Mage-OS 2.3.0 with \`vendor/mage-os/\` (388 packages) + \`vendor/hyva-themes/\` (10 packages)
- **Files:** 16,306 PHP files in scope-resolution, ~5,000+ class-like definitions

## Error output

```
████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  51% | Scope resolution (php): namespace siblings (16281 files)
<--- Last few GCs --->
[119108:0x43659000]  6272932 ms: Scavenge (interleaved) 32519.4 (32619.3) -> 32504.8 (32650.1) MB, pooled: 0 MB, 87.34 / 0.00 ms  (average mu = 0.160, current mu = 0.072) allocation failure; 
[119108:0x43659000]  6284843 ms: Mark-Compact (reduce) 32529.0 (32656.8) -> 32505.6 (32543.0) MB, pooled: 0 MB, 10962.74 / 0.00 ms

FATAL ERROR: Ineffective mark-compacts near heap limit Allocation failed - JavaScript heap out of memory
```

## Root cause analysis

### Step 3b (lines 224-243 of namespace-siblings.ts) — O(files × classDefs)

```typescript
// Cost: O(PHP files × class-like defs in the workspace) augmentation
// entries. Bounded and acceptable in practice — typical PHP projects
// have hundreds of files and classes, not tens of thousands.
for (const parsed of parsedFiles) {           // 16K files
    for (const [ns, bucket] of buckets) {     // hundreds of namespaces
        for (const def of bucket.classDefs) { // thousands of classes
            // Creates augmentation entry for EVERY file × EVERY FQN
            arr.push({ def, origin: 'namespace' });
        }
    }
}
```

The comment acknowledges the assumption: *"typical PHP projects have hundreds of files and classes, not tens of thousands."* Magento/Mage-OS violates this — 16K files × 5K+ class defs = **80M+ augmentation entries**, each holding a reference to a `SymbolDefinition` object. At ~400 bytes per entry, that's ~32GB.

### Step 4 (lines 254-301) — O(n²) parsedFiles.find()

```typescript
for (const parsed of parsedFiles) {              // 16K iterations
    for (const srcFilePath of accessibleFiles) {
        const srcParsed = parsedFiles.find(      // O(n) linear scan
            (p) => p.filePath === srcFilePath
        );
    }
}
```

`parsedFiles.find()` inside a nested loop is O(n²). For 16K files with hundreds of accessible siblings each, this is millions of linear scans.

## Proposed fix (not yet tested)

### Step 3b: Demand-driven FQN augmentation

Instead of injecting FQN bindings into every file's Module scope, only inject FQNs that each file actually references in its reference sites or type bindings:

```typescript
// Build FQN→def map once
const fqnDefs = new Map<string, SymbolDefinition[]>();
for (const [ns, bucket] of buckets) { /* ... build map ... */ }

// Only inject FQNs referenced by each file
for (const parsed of parsedFiles) {
    const referencedNames = new Set<string>();
    for (const ref of parsed.referenceSites) {
        if (ref.name?.includes('\\')) referencedNames.add(ref.name);
    }
    for (const scope of parsed.scopes) {
        for (const [name] of scope.typeBindings) {
            if (name.includes('\\')) referencedNames.add(name);
        }
    }
    // Only inject augmentations for FQNs this file actually uses
    for (const name of referencedNames) {
        const defs = fqnDefs.get(name.replace(/^\\/, ''));
        if (!defs) continue;
        // inject...
    }
}
```

This changes from O(files × classDefs) to O(files × refsPerFile), which is bounded by actual code references rather than workspace size.

### Step 4: Map-based lookup

Replace `parsedFiles.find()` with a pre-built `Map<string, ParsedFile>`:

```typescript
const parsedByPath = new Map<string, ParsedFile>();
for (const p of parsedFiles) parsedByPath.set(p.filePath, p);

// Then: parsedByPath.get(srcFilePath) instead of parsedFiles.find(...)
```

O(1) lookup instead of O(n) scan.

## Impact

This blocks indexing of any large PHP codebase with vendor dependencies:
- Magento 2 / Adobe Commerce / Mage-OS (300+ modules)
- Large Laravel projects with many Composer packages
- Any PHP project indexing \`vendor/\` for dependency analysis

## Workaround

None currently — even with 32GB heap the augmentation entries exhaust memory before scope-resolution completes.

